* this is a comment
* SNOBOL program consists of statements of the form
* label subject pattern = object : transfer
* so each statement can consist of five items, each item is optional
* this are just an assignments
    P = "abc"
    TEXT = "abcdef"
* if pattern P matches text, then jump to ABC_MATCHES, otherwise jump to END
    TEXT P : S(ABC_MATCHES) F(SPECIAL_VARIABLES)
* ABC_MATCHES is a label, jump without F/S is unconditional jump
ABC_MATCHES OUTPUT = "abc matches" : (SPECIAL_VARIABLES)

* SPECIAL_VARIABLES is a label
SPECIAL_VARIABLES
* OUTPUT is a special variable, this prints to stdout
    OUTPUT = "Hello, SNOBOL4!"

* INPUT is a special variable, this reads from stdin to X
    X = INPUT

* print X twice
    OUTPUT = X X

PATTERN_CONCAT
* this creates a pattern "abc abc"
    DOUBLE_ABC_WITH_SPACE = P " " P
    TEXT DOUBLE_ABC_WITH_SPACE : S(HAS_DOUBLE_ABC) F(COMPLEX_PATTERNS)
HAS_DOUBLE_ABC OUTPUT = "double abc matches"

COMPLEX_PATTERNS
* there are various ways to create complex patterns out of simple ones
* SPAN is like [0-9]+
    DIGITS = SPAN("0123456789")
* | is or
* POS(0) and RPOS(0) make a pattern to match an entire string, otherwise match would succeed
* if any part of the string matches the pattern
    FLOAT = POS(0) (DIGITS | DIGITS "." DIGITS) RPOS(0)
    "3.1415926" FLOAT : S(PI_IS_FLOAT) F(PI_IS_NOT_FLOAT)
PI_IS_FLOAT OUTPUT = "pi is float" : S(ASSIGNMENTS)
PI_IS_NOT_FLOAT OUTPUT = "pi is not float" : S(ASSIGNMENTS)

ASSIGNMENTS
* $ will assign match value to N, in this case it'll be 99 & problems
* $ will assign only if an entire pattern matches.
* There's also `.` that assigns even pattern matches partially
    "i have 99 problems" (DIGITS $ N) " " (ARB $ NOUN) RPOS(0)
    OUTPUT = "extracted number of " NOUN ": " N

REPLACEMENTS

* END is a label
END